## Basic Rules
 
 - Classes: PascalCase
 - Methods: PascalCase
 - Public properties: PascalCase
 - Private fields: _camelCase
 - Local variables: camelCase
 - Constants: PascalCase
 - Boolean names: use is, has, can, or should where appropriate.
 - One class per file.
 - File name matches the primary class.
 - Braces and indentation follow one consistent C# style.
 - Comments explain why, not obvious what.
 - Public systems/methods should have concise documentation explaining their purpose, inputs, outputs, and important behavior.
 - Don't leave commented-out code in committed code.
 - Avoid unexplained "magic numbers"; use named constants/configuration where appropriate.


 ## Interface Rules
 
  - All interfaces between systems are documented, especially inputs, outputs, and expected behaviors.
